+
+# Your own badges, defined once
+
+`labels.comp.md`, next to this demo, defines `bug`, `feature` and `chore`, each a `badge` with its colours, border and bold or italic text fixed. A document imports the file and uses them with nothing to configure.
+
+````compmd {render=both}
+---
+md:
+  import:
+    - from: ./labels.comp.md
+      names: [bug, feature, chore]
+---
+
+## Changes in 2.1
+
+- :feature[new] Saved searches, from the search page.
+- :feature[new] A map of the walks, each stop a pin.
+- :bug[bug] The tide table showed yesterday's tides after midnight.
+- :bug[bug] A walk's distance was in miles on a page set to kilometres.
+- :chore[chore] The photos are smaller, so the pages load faster.
+````
diff --git a/compmd-packs/badge/labels.comp.md b/compmd-packs/badge/labels.comp.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ad8382a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/compmd-packs/badge/labels.comp.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+md:
+  import:
+    - from: "@comp-markdown/badge@0"
+      names: [badge]
+  export:
+    names: [bug, feature, chore]
+---
+
+# A project's labels
+
+Three badges with their look fixed, defined once: a document imports this file and writes `:bug[bug]`, `:feature[new]` or `:chore[chore]`, nothing else.
+
+```compmd component=bug
+---
+:badge[**{{md.fallback}}**]{background="#ffebe9" border="1px solid #cf222e"}
+```
+
+```compmd component=feature
+---
+:badge[**{{md.fallback}}**]{background="#dafbe1" border="1px solid #1a7f37"}
+```
+
+```compmd component=chore
+---
+:badge[*{{md.fallback}}*]{background=subtle border=strong border-radius=s}
+```
